      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "History limitation: raw Iowa original-submission numerator counts could not be fetched through the web tool's dataset API or CSV access. historicalContext therefore contains nine fetched CMS snapshot percentages rounded to whole points, which are proxies for the target's exact one-decimal count ratios. No missing numerator counts or additional precision have been invented."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The reference class and outside-view base rate are nine consecutive Iowa original monthly shares from October 2025 through June 2026: their arithmetic mean is 59.1111%. March\u2013June averages 58.25%, supporting a modest downward level update. Momentum adjustment is zero because the January rise reversed in February and the latest four observations show no sustained trend. January remains in the dispersion sample; it is not treated as a confirmed reporting artifact."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Policy-mechanism adjustment is zero. Iowa HHS states that community-engagement requirements take effect December 1, 2026 for new applicants and apply to current members with renewal dates on or after February 2027. Those dates follow the August 2026 target cohort. Cohort composition and the success of automated eligibility matching remain relevant operational drivers."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: Use a damped persistence model anchored on the nine-month base rate, updating the level to an equal blend of June's 59% and the March\u2013June mean of 58.25%; point = 58.625%. Momentum, identified one-off, and direct policy adjustments are each zero. Successive changes are [-1, 3, 14, -19, 5, -1, -1, 2] percentage points, with mean 0.25 and squared deviations totaling 597.5. Sample sigma = 9.2389 percentage points, calculated as sqrt(597.5/7). The normal-approximation 80% one-month half-width is 1.28*sigma = 11.8258 points. Multiply by sqrt(2) for the two unobserved monthly transitions from June to August, giving 16.7242 points. Implied bounds are 41.9008% and 75.3492%, emitted as 41.9% and 75.3%. The widening retains the observed January\u2013February volatility."
      },
      {
        "kind": "math",
        "text": "Point = (59 + (59+58+57+59)/4)/2 = 58.625 -> 58.6. Half-width = 1.28*sqrt(597.5/7)*sqrt(2) = 16.7242. Interval = [58.625-16.7242, 58.625+16.7242] -> [41.9, 75.3]."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "An upside risk is a substantial improvement in automated matching or a cohort unusually easy to renew, which could lift the share above 75.3%. A downside risk is an eligibility-system disruption, more difficult verification cases, or classification of automated renewals under renewal-form outcomes, which could reduce the share below 41.9%. These concrete outcomes would land outside the interval."
      },
